-- title:
--   Descent to 𝔽_q of Frobenius-fixed modular functions
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$. Write $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k$ for the Laurent series $\mathsf{q}^{-1}\cdot(\text{the power series } \mathrm{jNum} \text{ with its integer coefficients mapped into } k)$ in $k((\mathsf{q}))$, and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,N$ for its image under the substitution `qExpand` at level $N$; the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ is by definition the intermediate field of $k((\mathsf{q}))/k$ generated by these two elements. Let $\bar g$ be an element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$ and assume that for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ the coefficient of $\mathsf{q}^n$ in $\bar g$ satisfies $c^q = c$, i.e. lies in the prime subfield of $k$. The conclusion is that $\bar g$ descends: there exists $h_0$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathbb{Z}/q)\,N$, the corresponding intermediate field of $(\mathbb{Z}/q)((\mathsf{q}))/(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, whose image under the coefficientwise ring homomorphism `coeffMap` induced by the canonical map $\mathbb{Z}/q \to k$ equals $\bar g$ as a Laurent series over $k$.
--
--   This is the descent of the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic $q$ to its $\mathbb{F}_q$-form: inside $k((\mathsf{q}))$, the elements of $k(\tilde j, \tilde j_N)$ with all $\mathsf{q}$-expansion coefficients in $\mathbb{F}_q$ come from $\mathbb{F}_q(\tilde j, \tilde j_N)$. It is used in the lifting of specializations of places, via [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_lift_of_coeff_pow_eq_of_forall_isAffineGeomPlace_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_lift_of_coeff_pow_eq_of_forall_isAffineGeomPlace_mem), and rests on the linear independence of coefficientwise images of linearly independent Laurent series.
